==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|invelop}}, {{l|en|invelope}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}
* {{l|en|envelope}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|envolupen}}, from {{der|en|fro|anveloper}}, {{m|fro|envoluper|}} (modern French {{m|fr|envelopper}}), from {{m|fro|en-}} + {{m|fro|voloper}}, {{m|fro|vloper||to wrap, wrap up}} (compare {{cog|it|viluppare|-viluppare}}; {{cog|roa-oit|-}} alternate form {{m|it|goluppare||to wrap}}) from {{der|en|VL.|*vuloppare||to wrap}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wlappaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*wrappaną||to wrap, roll up, turn, wind}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*werb-||to turn, bend}} [http://www.wordnik.com/words/envelop]. Akin to {{cog|enm|wlappen||to wrap, fold}} (Modern English {{m|en|lap||to wrap, involve, fold}}), Middle English {{m|enm|wrappen||to wrap}}, {{cog|dum|lappen||to wrap up, embrace}}, {{cog|da|-}} dialectal {{m|da|vravle||to wind, twist}}, {{cog|gml|wrempen||to wrinkle, distort}}, Old English {{m|ang|wearp||warp}}. Doublet of {{l|en|enwrap}}.

